A calendar item is something the assistant does or says at a moment of a day: an action it takes at its time
(the thermostat set at 9 PM), a reminder or a nudge to the owner at its time (coffee at 10 AM, the dog walk at
10 PM, timesheets in by 3 PM), preparation before a scheduled item. A habit at a time of day is an item: the
assistant reminds or nudges at its time.

A belief with nothing worth doing or saying at a time stays off the calendar: a standing state (a fan that
runs all the time, the house having one thermostat), how the owner is, a taste, how he likes to work.
A belief that limits, delays or makes an exception to another belief (its day, a limit, an exception, a
wish about reminders) is a condition on that belief, not an item of its own.
